Community 01 — V1 Client & Deployment Guide

Project

community-01 is a single-page premium community-platform marketing/showcase website for the fictional brand Orbit.

Orbit represents a place where people can discover interest-based communities, conversations, events, and other members.

This V1 is frontend-only. It does not include real authentication, database, community backend, chat engine, payments, or account creation.

Main V1 experience

The page communicates:

Discover communities

Browse interests/categories

See active discussions

Discover events

View member activity

Join Orbit through an interactive join modal

Use the main CTA to explore communities or start the join flow

Join Orbit flow

Join Orbit buttons open the reusable JoinModal component.

The modal lets a visitor choose:

Member / Creator / Organizer

Full name

Email address

Interests

The V1 submission is a frontend demo state only. It does not create or save a real account.

A future production version can connect the same UI to authentication, a database, or a membership API.

Header and navigation

The header is responsive across desktop, tablet, and mobile.

Desktop:

Orbit brand

Primary navigation

CTA buttons

Mobile/tablet:

Hamburger menu

Full navigation panel

CTA buttons

Escape closes the menu

Navigation closes the menu

Background scrolling is disabled while the menu is open

Always test the header at small widths such as 360px and 390px.

Visual design

Orbit uses a dark modern visual system with:

Strong typography

Purple/pink gradient accents

Soft borders

Rounded cards

Subtle glow effects

Responsive spacing

Interactive hover/focus states

The design is intended as a community-platform template, not a local-business website.

Categories and communities

Category cards such as Design & Art, Gaming, Fitness & Health, Music, Photography, and other interests are demo content.

Sample community names such as Golden Hour, Build Loop, Pixel Collective, and Nightfall Grid are also demo content.

For a real client, replace these with the client's actual community topics and names.

Client customization

Prefer centralized project data for client changes.

Review:

src/data/site.js

src/data/categories.js

src/data/images.js

public/images/

Update fictional Orbit branding and demo content when adapting the template.

Folder structure

Keep the project organized around reusable:

src/
├── components/
├── data/
├── pages/
├── sections/
├── styles/
└── main.jsx

public/
└── images/

Do not add unnecessary backend or application complexity to V1.

Local development

Install:

npm install

Run:

npm run dev

Expected:

http://localhost:5173/

Production preview:

npm run build
npm run preview

Expected:

http://localhost:4173/

Quality checklist

Before freezing, verify:

Responsive header works

Hamburger opens and closes correctly

Escape closes the menu

Navigation closes the menu

No horizontal overflow

Categories stay inside the viewport

Join Orbit opens the modal

Modal closes using X, backdrop, and Escape

Join form interaction works

Hero Join CTA opens the modal

Bottom Join CTA opens the modal

Images load correctly

No console errors during normal navigation

Test 360px, 390px, 430px, 768px, 1024px, 1280px, and large desktop widths

Then run:

npm run lint && npm run build

V1 boundary

The Join Orbit modal is a frontend demonstration, not real membership/authentication.

Future production functionality may include:

Authentication

Account creation

Database

Community membership

Discussions

Events

Notifications

Payments

Admin tools

These are outside this V1.

Freeze and Git

After runtime/mobile QA and a successful lint/build:

git add .
git commit -m "feat(community-01): finalize V1 community platform"
git push origin main

